# **This file is a security control, not only a build-speed one.**
#
# Docker sends the whole build context to the daemon, and anything COPY'd lands
# in an image layer permanently — deleting it in a later layer does not remove it
# from the image, it only hides it. A `.env` that reaches a layer is a leaked key
# (hard rule #2), so the secret-bearing entries below are load-bearing.

# --- secrets. Never in an image, never in the context. ---------------------- #
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/*.local.yaml

# --- the host's virtualenv --------------------------------------------------- #
# Built for macOS/arm64 against the host's interpreter. Copying it into a Linux
# image produces a venv whose binaries cannot run and whose .pth files point at
# paths that do not exist — and it would silently shadow the one uv builds.
.venv/
venv/

# --- regenerated or machine-local ------------------------------------------- #
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
graphify-out/

# `data/raw/` is the backfilled realized-vol series for the regime cold start
# (§4.3.1). Deliberately NOT baked in: it is regenerated with `make vrp` and goes
# stale daily, so compose mounts it as a volume instead. An image carrying a
# week-old series would look correct and reason from dead data.
data/raw/

# --- not needed at run time -------------------------------------------------- #
.git/
.github/
tests/
docs/
web/
*.md
!README.md
.DS_Store
